Implement Patient Data Management System Using Doubly Linked ListA hospital or clinic needs to maintain patient records such as Patient ID, Name, Age, andDisease. Since patients may be added or removed at any time, a dynamic data structure isrequired to manage the records efficiently.The problem is to design and implement a Patient Data Management System using a DoublyLinked List. Each node of the doubly linked list should store the details of one patient along withtwo pointers: Previous and Next, which connect the node to the preceding and succeedingpatient records.The system should allow the user to perform basic patient management operations such asadding a new patient, displaying patient records, searching for a patient, deleting a patientrecord, and displaying records in both forward and reverse directions.The implementation should maintain the links correctly after every insertion and deletionoperation and demonstrate the use of dynamic memory allocation and doubly linked listtraversal.
